# The DASHI integration / TOE spine

A single small spine that carries the corpus-wide cross-domain pass, rather than
a collection of per-domain reports.  Reading order:

1. `Integration.Levels` — the four-level classification (vocabulary, stored
   record dependency, shared implementation type, proved transport) as a Lean
   datatype, together with `Transport`, `NoTransport`, `Boundary` and `Socket`.
   Evidence constructors determine the level, so no row can be filed above the
   level it has a witness for.
2. `Integration.TernaryHub` — the corpus's six ternary carriers (`Trit`, the
   `Base369` tone, `Digit369`, the SSP trit carrier, the codec `TritCode`, the
   loom's `BTBranch`) are one object with one balanced coordinate, forced up to
   sign; every supplied polarity map becomes negation.
3. `Integration.Base369Group` — the 3/6/9 layer as finite cyclic groups: the
   loom's `projection2x3` realised as `ℤ/6 ≅ ℤ/2 × ℤ/3`, and the proof that the
   nonary layer is *not* two ternary layers.
4. `Integration.Address` — the prefix ultrametric on digit addresses, developed
   once for an arbitrary alphabet, with the codec-to-369 isometry.
5. `Integration.ClopenBalls` — supervoxel/clopen refinement: prefix balls are
   open and closed, refinement is exactly containment, no ball is atomic, and
   the corpus's clopen-authority record is a contentless socket.
6. `Integration.ReceiptSocket` — the archetypal receipt record and the exact
   sense in which it constrains nothing, plus the strengthened record that does.
7. `Integration.Refinement` — the corpus's never-instantiated refinement-system
   record, inhabited twice (dialectic loom, ternary addresses).
8. `Integration.MonsterFifteen` — the 15-prime mask ultrametric *is* the
   depth-15 prefix geometry, and the hyperfabric support map is a non-expansive
   but non-isometric, non-injective, non-homomorphic coarsening onto it.
9. `Integration.CognitionSupervoxel` — a cognition domain instance at the
   supervoxel junction: the phase-enriched trit, its constraint system, the
   proof that the "public zero" is not atomic (a `Bool` placeholder in the
   source), and the polarity-equivariance of the cognition observable.
10. `Integration.UltrametricCensus` — every live instance of the corpus's
   `Ultrametric` record is the same prefix geometry pulled back along a map,
   with one exception (the `Monster` walk distance) that provably is not.
11. `Integration.PhaseQuotient` — the corpus's nine-state carrier as the orbit
   space of a free `C₃` action on the 27 ternary endomorphism codes, its chart
   onto the `Base369` nonary labels, the *transported* exponent-three algebra
   those labels then carry, and the proof that the address carrier does not
   determine the algebra.  Also the two-origin dichotomy for `triXor`: additive
   in the native index chart, affine in the polarity-compatible balanced chart.
12. `Integration.SSPWeave` — the SSP orientation monoid, its `ℤ/2` quotient, and
   the functorial transport `T_{q∘p} = T_q ∘ T_p` on lane states, whose carrier
   is the ternary hub: the algebra the 15-lane layer does preserve.
13. `Integration.ObserverQuotient` — what the Boolean observer keeps (the
   symmetry action, uniquely descending) and what it forgets (the sign, and any
   binary law at all), plus the signed relational defect layer on which the
   preserved algebra lives.
14. `Integration.PolarResidual` — the residual-bearing 9 → 6 projection as an
   exact `9 ≃ 6 + 3` equivalence, with the impossibility of a direct retraction.
15. `Integration.ResidualQuotient` — the "coarse state + retained residual
   reopens the rich state" pattern as one structure, with the polar projection
   and the magnitude observer as proved instances, and one lemma explaining why
   the residual is never removable.
16. `Integration.SymmetryReduction` — "symmetry reduction" as a typed
   obligation: `EquivariantQuotient` bundles an action on each layer with the
   commuting square `π (g · x) = ḡ · π x`.  Inhabited by the free `C₃`
   27 → 9 phase reduction, by the polarity/magnitude observer, and by one
   instance with nontrivial induced action; and the native-chart support
   observer is shown to admit no such structure at all.
17. `Integration.Registry` — the checked global registry: positive rows with
   their evidence, negative rows with their refutations, sockets with their
   underdetermination proofs.
18. `Integration.RiemannReflection`, `Integration.RiemannStrip`,
   `Integration.RiemannSubstrate`, `Integration.RiemannXiSymmetry` — the RH/zeta
   *analytic* lane brought into the
   same vocabulary: the lane's reflection and three-phase carriers as hub
   transports, the critical line as the fixed locus of the lane's involution
   with the displacement as the kernel's transverse coordinate, and the analytic
   substrate tower classified as a socket (both truth values of its own
   `RiemannHypothesisFor` occur among its inhabitants).  `RiemannXiSymmetry`
   adds the rational critical-plane `QCoord` with its three involutions, the
   injective evaluation `qToC` into `ℂ` that intertwines all three, and the
   xi-zero-symmetry and Hilbert–Pólya interfaces, both shown to be sockets.
19. `Integration.RiemannDomain` — the analytic domain's rows, boundaries and
   sockets, plus the checked summary bundle.  No statement about the Riemann
   zeta function, its zeros or the Riemann hypothesis is made anywhere.
20. `Integration.AxiomAudit` — `#print axioms` for every headline result.

Provenance: `Lean/AgdaMirror/*` are hand-transcribed Lean mirrors of named Agda
modules; the Agda sources are read-only here (no Agda toolchain is available in
this environment, so no Agda file is claimed to have been rechecked).  Every
statement in this spine is a Lean statement about Lean definitions.

Scope: no Yang–Mills or Navier–Stokes material is imported or referenced.  No
physical, empirical, Monster-group, moonshine, vertex-algebra, unitarity or
Riemann-hypothesis claim is made.  Outside the analytic lane (items 18–19) every
carrier is finite and every distance is a natural number; inside it the carriers
are `ℝ` and `ℂ` as sets with involutions, and no analytic hypothesis is
discharged.
-/
